<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madanapala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 1161</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madanapala was the last important king of the Pala dynasty of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, reigning in the mid-12th century. By his time the Palas had lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sena-dynasty">Sena dynasty</a> and held only parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a>, and his death around 1161 is taken as the end of Pala rule.</p></div>
